{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1427986143,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3MTc3OTE5Mg=="},"added":["annex"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1427986568,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg4OTM1NjQ1","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-88935645"},"message":"Forgot version info:\n\n```\ngit annex version\ngit-annex version: 5.20150327+git27-g6af24b6-1~nd80+1\nbuild flags: Assistant Webapp Webapp-secure Pairing Testsuite S3 WebDAV Inotify DBus DesktopNotify XMPP DNS Feeds Quvi TDFA\nkey/value backends: SHA256E SHA1E SHA512E SHA224E SHA384E SKEIN256E SKEIN512E MD5E SHA256 SHA1 SHA512 SHA224 SHA384 SKEIN256 SKEIN512 MD5 WORM URL\nremote types: git gcrypt S3 bup directory rsync web bittorrent webdav tahoe glacier ddar hook external\nlocal repository version: 5\nsupported repository version: 5\nupgrade supported from repository versions: 0 1 2 4\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1428458966,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkwNzgwNzgz","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-90780783"},"message":"@joeyh could you please have a look at the above report with some awkward behavior via direct mode proxy?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1428524260,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkxMDI0Mjc0","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-91024274"},"message":"\u003e pathspec '.' did not match any file(s) known to git\n\nThis is because there's no branch available yet at this point, and\ngit-annex proxy checks out the current branch. I could probably work\naround this by having it detect this case and set up the same state in\nits temporary work tree. However, it's hard to think of something\ngit-annex proxy could actually be useful for in this early situation\n(see below).\n\n\u003e fatal: pathspec 'testfile2' did not match any files\n\nThis is because git-annex proxy sets up a temporary work tree and runs\nthe git command in there. But files not yet added to git are not present\nin that temporary work tree.\n\n\u003e fatal: /home/ben/Development/testannex/testfile2: '/home/ben/Development/testannex/testfile2' is outside repository\n\nAgain due to the temporary work tree.\n\nYou don't actually need git-annex proxy in this situation. It would work to\nrun \"git -c core.bare=false add testfile2\". Since git add does\nnot update the work tree, it is safe to bypass the direct mode guard this way\nin this case.\n\nI can't see a good way to make git-annex proxy support this case, and it's\nnot the kind of use case I had in mind for it, quite.\n\nI think that the best way to improve git-annex though, would be to\nmake `git-annex add` not just skip over files that annex.largefiles\ndoesn't match (the current behavior), but instead add them to git as\nregular non-annexed files. I've made this change in git..\n\n```\njoey@darkstar:~/tmp/d\u003eecho hi \u003e testfile3\njoey@darkstar:~/tmp/d\u003egit config annex.largefiles\nlargerthan=100kb\njoey@darkstar:~/tmp/d\u003egit annex add testfile3\nadd testfile3 (non-large file; adding to git directly) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n```\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1428565627,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkxMTQxNTQy","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-91141542"},"message":"Thank you, @joeyh. \n\n\u003e You don't actually need git-annex proxy in this situation. It would work to\n\u003e run \"git -c core.bare=false add testfile2\". Since git add does\n\u003e not update the work tree, it is safe to bypass the direct mode guard this way\n\u003e in this case.\n\nOk. So may be that's the way to go.\n\n\u003e I think that the best way to improve git-annex though, would be to\n\u003e make `git-annex add` not just skip over files that annex.largefiles\n\u003e doesn't match (the current behavior), but instead add them to git as\n\u003e regular non-annexed files. I've made this change in git..\n\nThis is nice to have, but I think the file size itself will not be the actual criteria in our case.\nAnyway, I'll give it a try using the way you proposed above.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1428596734,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkxMjgwNzQ3","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-91280747"},"message":"Joey Hess wrote:\n\n\u003e This is because there's no branch available yet at this point, and\n\u003e git-annex proxy checks out the current branch. I could probably work\n\u003e around this by having it detect this case and set up the same state in\n\u003e its temporary work tree. However, it's hard to think of something\n\u003e git-annex proxy could actually be useful for in this early situation\n\u003e (see below).\n\nI thought of some things. :) Checking out a branch, for example.\n\nSo, I've fixed git annex proxy in a newly created repository.\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1428597081,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkxMjgzNDQ4","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-91283448"},"message":"@bpoldrack you can use other criteria than size, like extension or location.\n\nYou could even do this to force git annex add to add the file content to git:\n\ngit -c annex.largefiles='exclude=*' annex add foo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1428659468,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkxNDk4NDU0","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/97#issuecomment-91498454"},"message":"Thanks again!\n\n\u003e You could even do this to force git annex add to add the file content to git:\n\u003e git -c annex.largefiles='exclude=*' annex add foo\n\nMay be this will become useful at some point, but for now I will stay with \"git -c core.bare=false add foo\".\nEspecially because that way foo remains \"unknown\" to git-annex in the sense, that \"git annex find\" won't list it as well as \"git annex lookupkey foo\" returns nothing. So, there is an easy way to know whether a file belongs to git itself or git-annex and this behaviour is consistent with doing the same in indirect mode. When using git annex add to add to git directly, this behaviour changes. This would have been the same if my original approach was working, I guess - I just didn't think of it.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1428923502,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Mjc5NjUyNjU5"},"status":2}]}